msclap-infer is an independent, inference-only distribution of the 2023
Microsoft CLAP audio/text encoder. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by
Microsoft.

The following model implementation files are adapted from the MIT-licensed
Microsoft CLAP project (msclap 1.3.4):
  src/msclap_infer/_impl/clap.py
  src/msclap_infer/_impl/htsat.py
  src/msclap_infer/_impl/audio.py
  src/msclap_infer/_impl/config.py
  src/msclap_infer/_impl/pytorch_utils.py

Changes: inference-only extraction; pinned GPT-2 config instead of loading
pretrained GPT-2 parameters; removal of the torchlibrosa dependency via a
pure-PyTorch frozen STFT/log-mel frontend; training and captioning surfaces
are excluded. The original project is at https://github.com/microsoft/CLAP.

No model weights are bundled. The 2023 checkpoint is downloaded separately
from microsoft/msclap under its model-card license (MS-PL). GPT-2 configuration
and tokenizer files are downloaded from the MIT-licensed GPT-2 model repository.
The package code's MIT license does not change the terms for downloaded assets.
